From 251f7af47ae6185a6af0866aab9ad1034fedf4f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:50:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): cache SP local routing masks and skip SP tail
 pad rows in partials router

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488. It applies unchanged on candidate-49's 0762..0766, which touch neither file.

Rationale:
During sequence-parallel prefill on the 20 encoder layers (0..19), mhc.post_pre casts each rank's L = ceil(T / TP) shard to MXFP8 while sp_moe_inputs calls router.route_local(x, sp_rows, input_ids=input_ids) before sp_rows.gather_mxfp8(x_q, weights, ids):
1. While _routing_masks cached the full T-row image and routed masks on ForwardContext, _local_mask(mask, rows, sp_rows) called sp_rows.local_slice(mask[:sp_rows.num_tokens]) uncached on every encoder layer. Whenever T % TP != 0 (every power-of-2 chunk size T = 256..16384 on TP=3, and any non-multiple of TP on TP=4), the tail rank (rank = TP - 1, where real_rows < local_rows) allocated a new boolean tensor and copied [:real_rows] twice per layer (4 GPU kernel launches per layer, 80 across the 20 encoder layers), adding 8.7-20.5 us/layer (+3% to +44% local router latency) on the tail rank immediately before the synchronous gather_mxfp8 collective.
2. In _partials_mask (used by TileLangGateRouter when local_rows <= 256, i.e., 205 <= T <= 768 on TP=3 and 205 <= T <= 1024 on TP=4), _local_mask(is_padding, rows, sp_rows) zero-padded [real_rows:local_rows] with False (active / route) instead of True (padding / skip), causing route_partials to route unused SP tail pad rows as active tokens (and fail T.device_assert(finite) if tail pad rows contained NaN/Inf) instead of skipping them with topk_idx = -1, topk_weights = 0.0 as TileKernelsRouter does when local_rows > 256.

Keep the tail rank's _local_mask slices on the forward's ForwardContext, keyed by the mask tensor (held by the entry, so its id cannot be reused while the entry lives) and (num_tokens, world_size, rank, rows, pad), and pass pad=True in _partials_mask so SP tail pad rows [real_rows:local_rows] are padded with True (skipped).

A rank without pad rows keeps nothing. Its slice is a view of the mask, which _local_mask now makes directly, mask[start:start + local_rows] (the very view sp_rows.local_slice(mask[:num_tokens]) returns), with one slice instead of two and without building a key or touching the context. On sp8 the host cost of one routing layer's local masks on such a rank is 2.8-3.1 us under inference mode and 3.6-3.9 us under no_grad, against 4.9-5.3 us and 6.4-6.8 us in 1107; on the tail rank it is 2.2-2.3 us under either, against 21.1-21.3 us and 23.9-24.5 us. The GPU work of a rank without pad rows is 1107's.

The key reads no version counter. The vLLM worker runs every forward, its startup memory profile included, under torch.inference_mode, where the step's masks are inference tensors that track none: the first revision validated entries with mask._version, which raised "Inference tensors do not track version counter" in _local_mask on every SP route_local call and stopped the engine from booting (candidate-49, tp3-switched, profile_run). A rank without pad rows cannot see a stale mask: it keeps nothing, and makes its view from the mask it is handed on every call, as 1107 does. A slice the tail rank keeps cannot be stale either: a forward's padding mask and ids are filled before it runs and do not change while it runs (the routed and image masks 1107 already keeps on ForwardContext, keyed by tensor identity alone, rely on the same), the routed and image masks are new tensors each forward that nothing writes after their kernel, and the runner creates a new ForwardContext for every forward, so a slice never outlives its forward, even though the runner's persistent buffers keep their storage across steps. Outside a forward nothing is cached: the first revision fell back to caching on sp_rows, but SPRows is a frozen dataclass (assigning raised FrozenInstanceError) and a value shared by equal layouts, not a step.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal) on all real rows [0:real_rows] across all ranks and chunk sizes, under torch.inference_mode as under no_grad; skips unused SP tail pad rows [real_rows:local_rows] with topk_idx = -1 and topk_weights = 0.0 in route_partials (matching TileKernelsRouter).

Tests:
- New: test_gate_router_route_local_under_inference_mode (TP3 T=205, 800, 1024 and TP4 T=1024, every rank, 3 layers a forward, bit-equal to the no_grad route; only the tail rank keeps masks, where the previous revision asserted that every rank keeps them), test_gate_router_route_local_masks_last_one_forward (persistent padding and id buffers refilled in place across three forwards, each routed with its own masks), test_gate_router_route_local_outside_a_forward (no ForwardContext). All six fail on the first revision (5 RuntimeError, 1 FrozenInstanceError) and pass on this one.
- New: test_local_mask_keeps_only_the_tail_ranks_slices (TP3 T=205, 800, 1024 and TP4 T=1024, every rank, masks of T and T + 5 rows, pad and no pad, under inference mode): a rank without pad rows gets local_slice's own view (same base, data pointer and strides) and keeps nothing; the tail rank's slice is a new tensor, its pad rows set with pad, kept and handed back; a mask shorter than T is refused as local_slice refuses it.
- pytest --noconftest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_router.py (279 passed on each of 2 fresh container boots).

Upstream status: local SP prefill router optimization and tail-padding fix for DeepSeek V4.1 TileLang router.
